    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170-a7">

                <pb facs="0440" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg344"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 9 in No. 811.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. Shinagawa.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-08-19"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 19,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7464.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your letter of yesterday.
                    As the matter of the arrest of General Le Gendre is stated by you to be the
                    subject of correspondence between our respective governments, I will transmit a
                    copy of the order upon which he was released to Washington.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEORGE F. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
